AB  - The rapid advancement in large language models (LLMs) has demonstrated their significant potential to function as intelligent assistants across diverse application domains. Despite their impressive reasoning capabilities, most existing LLM-based systems are designed as generic models and exhibit limited ability to adapt the specific knowledge requirements, preferences, and communication styles of individual users. This limitation reduces their effectiveness in domain where personalization is essential, such as education, healthcare, professional consulting, and personal productivity. To address this challenge, this paper proposes Intellicore, a novel framework for developing personalized AI assistants using the Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) approach. This proposed framework integrates both user-specific and domain-specific data sources with optimized retrieval processes. It enables the generation of responses that are contextually relevant, accurate and tailored to individual users. Intellicore emphasizes a modular architecture by incorporating document embedding, semantic search, and adaptive prompt engineering, and efficient fine-tuning techniques, thereby ensuring scalability across multiple users and applications. Unlike conventional chatbot platforms, Intellicore ensures response consistency by grounding generation in authoritative external knowledge sources while simultaneously adapting to the user context. The paper further details the implementation of the proposed framework, including use of vector databases, orchestration layers, and metrics for evaluating personalization quality. The initial empirical results indicate that Intellicore significantly improves accuracy and user satisfaction when compared to standard LLM-based chatbots. Overall, this study presents a practical and extensible framework for building next-generation AI assistants that effectively balance general intelligence with user-specific personalization, laying the groundwork for future applications in interactive intelligent systems.
