AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) achieve strong results on knowledge-intensive tasks but remain prone to hallucinations in domain-specific question-answering tasks. Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) mitigates this issue by leveraging external knowledge; however, it suffers from noisy retrieval results and faces difficulty in balancing denoising with information retention. To address these challenges, we propose KRPKIRAG, a novel question answering framework that integrates Knowledge Refinement and Potential Knowledge Integration for Retrieval-Augmented Generation. The system first employs a knowledge refinement module to filter noisy passages while retaining high-value content. Subsequently, it applies potential knowledge integration to re-examine passages initially deemed noisy or ambiguous to determine whether they should be retained. Experiments on multiple question-answering datasets demonstrate consistent improvements in F1 and Exact Match (EM) scores, highlighting the effectiveness and generalizability of the proposed method.
