AB  - Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) serves as a novel framework that enhances factual correctness and contextual appropriateness of large language model (LLM) outputs through its integration of document retrieval systems that access modern and updated external content. Our team developed an RAG pipeline that utilizes Lang Chain and Chroma DB alongside the Falcon-7B-Instruct model from Hugging Face as its core components. The pipeline starts by processing user-defined textual information and turns it into overlapped sections. A state-of-the-art transformer embedding model converts the input chunks into dense vector embeddings which get stored in a vector database. A retriever identifies semantic text fragments that best match the query while a specific prompt template adds retrieved contextual fragments to the input. After retrieval of context, the LLM returns an answer that is brief with factual evidence. The document provides thorough descriptions of the extended introduction section and methodology along with a detailed survey of important publications that shaped our method.
ER  - 

