AB  - Aiming at the problems of large volume and frequent updates of enterprise rules and regulations documents, low efficiency of traditional static document retrieval, and susceptibility to misunderstanding, an intelligent question answering system for rules and regulations based on large language models and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) technology is designed. The core contribution lies in the optimization of the retrieval stage: a clause-number-aware adaptive two-level chunking strategy is proposed to ensure semantic integrity; a dual-path hybrid retrieval architecture combining BM25 keyword search and BGE vector retrieval is designed; and a query-type-driven weighted reciprocal rank fusion (RRF) algorithm is introduced for adaptive fusion of retrieval results. For multi-turn dialogue scenarios, a query completion mechanism combining rule-based routing and LLM-based rewriting is designed. The system is built on the LangChain framework for document processing and workflow orchestration, uses Ollama for local deployment of the Qwen3.5:2B model for answer generation, employs Redis cache for response speed optimization, and uses Streamlit to build a visual interactive interface. A test set containing 120 questions covering five types of policy scenarios (attendance, performance, reimbursement, etc.) is constructed. Experimental results show that hybrid retrieval achieves a hit rate of 95.0% under standard queries and 85.0% under colloquial queries. Compared with single-path FAISS retrieval, it improves by 2.5 percentage points under standard queries and decreases by 7.5 percentage points under colloquial queries. Notably, in colloquial scenarios, Whoosh returns low-relevance but non-empty results that interfere with the fused ranking, causing the hybrid hit rate (85.0%) to fall below that of FAISS alone (92.5%); this is a known limitation and a key direction for future optimization, although the first-hit rate remains above 70%). The question answering accuracy reaches 87.5%, and the response time after cache hit is below 0.1 seconds. The system verifies the effectiveness of the hybrid retrieval RAG architecture in enterprise rules and regulations QA scenarios, providing a feasible path for transforming enterprise document management from static storage to intelligent services.
ER  - 

