AB  - Driven by global energy transition and digital transformation, the complexity of power grid dispatching and control has increased sharply, making traditional rule-based question answering systems incompetent for professional accurate decision-making. Focusing on the core pain points of this field such as strong data professionalism, high real-time requirements, complex business scenarios, this paper researches and implements a large language model (LLM)-based knowledge question answering system. We first construct a multi-source heterogeneous data processing system and domain knowledge base, realizing efficient knowledge representation and retrieval via the BERT-MIL model and Milvus vector database. Then, based on the 20B power-specialized State Grid “Guangming LLM”, we optimize its domain adaptability through knowledge distillation and contrastive learning, and design a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture. Finally, a three-level technical framework (data-model-application) and a closed-loop question answering system are built. Experimental results show the system achieves 92% accuracy, 2.3s average response time, and over 90% knowledge coverage, significantly improving dispatching decision efficiency and providing technical support for intelligent upgrading of power grid dispatching and control in new power systems.
