AB  - In the Transnational Education (TNE) context, scattered sources and multi-institutional governance structures create some hardship for students to access information for support. Aimed at the Hainan Lingshui campus, this paper introduces the development of an AI-driven chatbot prototype based on Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to address some key issues faced by students in obtaining accurate and timely information. The developed prototype adopts an automated multi-source data crawling and processing pipeline, integrates the PostgreSQL vector database, and leverages hybrid retrieval techniques combined with Large Language Models (LLMs) to realize unified integration and accurate response generation. Empirical evaluation demonstrates that the developed system achieves an 87.5% task success rate and reduces information retrieval time by 81.8% compared to traditional manual methods, effectively mitigating hallucinations through a precisely tuned hybrid retrieval strategy.
