AB  - More than 3.5 billion people in the world are still affected by healthcare gaps, especially where access to proper medical diagnosis is difficult. This work presents a multimodal AI-powered healthcare chatbot that understands both textual and image-based symptoms. The proposed chatbot, developed using a BioMistral-7B Q4 quantized large language model and further augmented with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), reduces hallucinations and provides medically found responses. Leveraging data from the WHO Global Health Observatory (GHO)[10] and a carefully curated symptomdisease dataset, it delivers trustworthy diagnostic suggestions. Compared to baseline LLMs, the system achieved 95% F1-score in matching symptom-disease, 87% diagnostic accuracy, with an 83% reduction in hallucinations. The results have confirmed the system's ability to deliver equitable and reliable medical care in resource-poor settings.
