AB  - We present a multimodal retrieval system that integrates CLIP-based encoding, FAISS indexing, and large language model (LLM) enhancement for cross-modal search and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG). In the retrieval aspect, the system supports text-to-image, image-to-image, and image-to-text search within a unified framework. In the query understanding aspect, the LLM reformulates multilingual user queries into English visual descriptions aligned with CLIP, enabling cross-lingual retrieval over English image collections without model retraining. Compared with conventional CLIP-based retrieval systems, this system improves accessibility for multilingual users while preserving efficient real-time search. The system further supports natural language question answering through an RAG pipeline grounded in retrieved visual evidence with explicit citations. The demonstration features live interactive search and question answering, showcasing cross-lingual retrieval and multimodal question answering capabilities. Source code: https://github.com/dticpw/multimodal-retrieval
