AB  - The university recruitment process in the case of academic institutions is a critical but is always full of decentralized workflow, manual student information management, and insufficient specialist advising tools. Even though various intelligent systems have been created to address these dilemmas, the majority of them are autonomous and they exist on the single aspects. Consequently, the current solutions are expected to cope with limited actions, including simple access to data or predictive algorithms, instead of providing a user-friendly and holistic recruitment environment. This paper proposes Smart Placement Assistance, a unified web-based platform with three primary components: a Placement Dashboard, a Company Insights module, and an AI driven chatbot built on a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework. The system works cutting-edge technology, such as the Gemma Large Language Model (LLM) applied by Ollama to enable context-aware responses and semantic search, and Chroma DB for vector-based data storage. According to experimental results, the proposed architecture improves student access to relevant placement-related insights while also lowering information retrieval latency.
