AB  - Cardiovascular disease remains a leading cause of global mortality, highlighting the need for intelligent and reliable clinical decision support systems. This paper presents the research and implementation of a cardiovascular question answering system based on Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) and Knowledge Graphs (KG). The proposed framework integrates dense and hybrid retrieval, structured knowledge graph reasoning, evidence re-ranking, and chain-of-thought generation to enhance answer accuracy, interpretability, and clinical consistency. Extensive experiments, including survival analysis, multi-type question answering evaluation, ablation studies, and system-level ROC and PR analyses, demonstrate that the proposed method significantly outperforms RAG-only, KG-only, and LLM-only baselines. The results confirm that combining retrieval-based evidence with explicit knowledge graph reasoning provides a robust and explainable solution for cardiovascular clinical question answering.
