AB  - This study explored an AI teaching assistant system that utilizes LoRA fine-tuning of large language models (LLMs) combined with LangChain technology to improve accuracy in specialized areas like software testing. Employing Agent agents and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), the research demonstrated the feasibility of knowledge-based intelligent question-answering. Initially, relevant technologies such as model fine-tuning and knowledge vector databases were compared, followed by the creation of a software testing dataset from the ISTQB question bank. The system was designed using Qwen-1.8B-Chat and LoRA fine-tuning, with a knowledge vector database built for course information. Agent agents were developed to integrate a local search engine (SearXNG). Testing showed that the fine-tuned LLM significantly improved question-answering accuracy, as measured by BLEU and ROUGE metrics, and the Agent successfully retrieved information from both the search engine and knowledge database. However, the study identified areas for improvement in LLM optimization and knowledge base completeness.
