AB  - Traditional question-answering (QA) systems in multilingual classrooms struggle when handling Arabic, French, and English instructions alongside complex mathematical notation in Moroccan curricula. This study introduces an advanced trilingual Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) framework for curriculum-based QA across these three languages. The proposed approach combines specialized document parsing with right-to-left text handling, staged evaluation of Naive, Hybrid, and Advanced RAG models, and advanced techniques such as query expansion, rank fusion, reranking, and confidence scoring to reduce LLM hallucinations. Using dual retrieval (dense and sparse), multi-stage ranking, multilingual embeddings, and DeepSeek R1 for generation, the Advanced pipeline achieves near-perfect embedding similarity (0.95+ correctness, 0.93+ faithfulness) and strong trilingual performance, with Arabic queries reaching French-level accuracy. The results highlight a practical, context-aware solution for multilingual educational QA. Future work will explore Agentic RAG architectures to address reasoning gaps and multi-turn dialogue.
