AB  - To address the shortage of medical personnel and the increasing demand for health consultation, we present a multi-modal intelligent health education robot based on Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG). The proposed system integrates a large language model with a FAISS vector database, Microsoft Azure Speech Services, and a Unity-based 3D virtual avatar to enable natural speech-based interaction. By grounding responses in a verified internal medical knowledge base, the RAG mechanism improves response reliability and mitigates hallucination issues commonly observed in conventional Large Language Models. The system is designed to provide accessible and easy-to-understand medical guidance, particularly for elderly users and patients with limited literacy, while reducing repetitive educational workloads for medical staff. This work demonstrates the feasibility of applying multi-modal LLM-based systems to practical smart healthcare applications.
