AB  - This paper presents Fintellect, a personal tutor chatbot designed to assist students at the Faculty of Computer Science and Engineering (FCSE) by providing fast, reliable, and context-aware answers to course-related queries. Fintellect integrates a web-based chat interface with a two-backend architecture: a service for managing application logic and persistent chat history, and a service for retrieval and response generation. Course materials, including lectures, exercises, labs, and past exams, are preprocessed into a vector database to enable semantic retrieval of relevant context, which grounds responses generated by a large language model. This work is positioned primarily as a system design and implementation paper: our goal is to present the architecture, core design decisions, and engineering trade-offs involved in building an educational RAG application in a faculty setting. We describe the system architecture, implementation details, and key design decisions, demonstrating how Retrieval-Augmented Generation can support interactive, context-aware educational applications.
