AB  - Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) enhances Large Language Models (LLMs) with external knowledge, making it a highly promising technology for dynamic campus information systems. However, conventional RAG systems lack user personalization and document version control, often leading to generic responses and the risk of retrieving outdated academic regulations. To resolve these issues, this study proposes an enhanced RAG architecture that integrates user personalization and knowledge base versioning through persona metadata and semantic versioning (X.Y.Z) utilizing a hybrid SQL-vector search mechanism. Experimental results demonstrate that the proposed approach successfully isolates context according to user roles (e.g., lecturers and students) and consistently retrieves the most accurate, up-to-date document versions while significantly optimizing search space and reducing system latency.
